# Review routing, and — more importantly — a record of who owns what.
#
# Neglect, not modelling error, is the most likely way this register dies (see
# docs/background.md). If a section below has no owner, that is a finding, not a
# formatting problem. See docs/open-questions.md Q8.

# Schema, tooling, and implementation decisions
/bin/                   @rainhead
/.github/               @rainhead
/decisions/             @rainhead
/data/sources.tsv       @rainhead

# Domain content. Needs scientific review; software review is not sufficient.
#
# WARNING: as written, these lines do the OPPOSITE of what the comment says. Every path
# below is assigned to a software reviewer, so domain content currently merges without
# any domain review at all. This is not a formatting gap — it is the mis-routing itself.
# Until a scientific reviewer is named (Q8), treat any change to these paths as blocked
# on out-of-band review, because CODEOWNERS will not ask for it.
# TODO(Q8): add @scottveirs and other scientific reviewers once confirmed.
/definitions/           @rainhead
/data/entities.tsv      @rainhead
/data/membership.tsv    @rainhead
/data/status.tsv        @rainhead
/data/names.tsv         @rainhead
/data/ranks.tsv         @rainhead
